From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree: a hosting program's AppDomainManager, default domain properties and event actions

ICLRControl::GetCLRManager now hands out ICLROnEventManager and ICLRDomainManager.
- ICLROnEventManager keeps the registered actions. Mono reports no such events to the host.
- ICLRDomainManager takes the AppDomainManager type and the properties of the default domain.
When the default domain starts:
- Its properties are set (AppDomain.SetData).
- The manager is made, its InitializeNewDomain runs, and it becomes the domain's manager.
- The host is told through IHostControl::SetAppDomainManager.
- A configuration file the manager gives the domain becomes the one the domain binds by: its
  privatePath, binding redirects and code bases, and Mono's own configuration.
A managed exception that a hosting call runs into is logged (warn+mscoree).
